# R44 Track E — a `meta` constant used as an ARRAY SIZE in a LOCAL DECLARATION.
#
# AXIS: array-size position. This fixture samples the LOCAL-VARIABLE cell.
# Siblings (same axis, other cells):
#   meta_const_array_size_param.gg    — function PARAMETER type
#   meta_const_array_size_return.gg   — function RETURN type
#   the STRUCT-FIELD cell is NOT covered: `struct S: int[3] data` is
#   check-clean but fails the C compile even with a LITERAL size, a separate
#   pre-existing defect filed in TODO.md ("struct field of fixed-array type").
#
# RED-VERIFIED at HEAD 4a16e4c5 (pre-fix): `gg check` rc 1,
#   `type mismatch: expected `int[0]`, found `int[3]``
# because `meta.rs:1894 substitute_type` dropped the SIZE expression of
# `Type::Array` on the floor, so `N` never became `3` and `types.rs`
# resolved the unevaluated size to 0.
#
# ⚠ WHY THIS LIVES IN `known_gaps/` DESPITE PASSING: placement, not status.
# `runtime_parity_corpus` (tests/integration.rs) auto-scans every TOP-LEVEL
# `tests/fixtures/*.gg`, and the self-host lane cannot compile this shape at
# all — its parser has NO `Type[N]` array-type production, so `int[N]` in a
# type position parses as `TNamed("int", [N])` (generic arguments) and
# `TArray` is never constructed from source. A top-level row would therefore
# be own-round non-MATCH inflow against `RUNTIME_DIFF_NONMATCH_CEILING`,
# which Core #9 ⊕ forbids outright. The test below is LIVE, not `#[ignore]`d:
# the Rust behaviour asserted here is the CORRECT behaviour and a regression
# goes red immediately. Promote to top-level the moment the self-host lane
# grows fixed-size array types (filed in TODO.md).
meta int N = 3

int main():
    int[N] a = [10, 20, 30]
    print(a[0] + a[1] + a[2])
    return 0
